{"game": "risk-of-rain-2013", "language": "english", "appid": 248820, "month": "2020-10", "window": 2, "start_date": 1602115200, "end_date": 1602806399, "month_true_total": 52, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-07 09:18:24 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "77583153", "author": {"steamid": "76561198021223998", "personaname": "Z's Ghost", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198021223998/", "num_games_owned": 476, "num_reviews": 23, "playtime_forever": 1975, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1556, "last_played": 1782004270, "avatar": "dc713fb642e779b46baed3468c4060ff3fc75355"}, "language": "english", "review": "Without foreknowledge, this game is barely playable.\nIn order to play effectively on anything but drizzle difficulty, one needs to rush to find the teleporter as soon as possible. This is because the run tends towards failure if you average more than about five minutes on stages. Knowing this makes all the difference in the experience.\nUnfortunately, this is rather counterintuitive, so new players are bound to prioritize the looting aspect of the gameplay loop. Given how loot defines runs, it's not something to neglect, and so this ironically creates a very--shall we say--\"esoteric\" filter, as one must defy that instinct to have any hope for success.\nKudos to anyone who figured out the five minute rule on their own.\n\nThat said, I still think the soundtrack is probably the best part of the game.", "timestamp_created": 1602740479, "timestamp_updated": 1780639099, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": "0.308246612548828125", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1383930480", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 3, "count": 3}]}, {"recommendationid": "77581876", "author": {"steamid": "765611983212975